id=dirtysepbypass
name=DirtySepolicy Bypass
version=v5.0.0
versionCode=50000
author=SHuiTU68
description=Kernel-side hiding (no Zygisk): a small kprobe LKM hides Magisk/LSPosed/KernelSU/APatch SELinux contexts, fakes selinuxfs access answers and drops root-managed mount lines for ordinary apps. Nothing is injected into app, zygote or app_zygote processes, so isolated probes are covered too. Requires an arm64 device whose kernel allows kretprobes and unsigned module loading (OnePlus MT6991 / 6.6 GKI).
updateJson=
